# Everything here is deployed to a Linux box (Venus OS, armv7l). A CRLF in a
# `#!/bin/sh` line makes the kernel look for an interpreter called "/bin/sh\r"
# and the service never starts, so keep LF in the WORKING TREE too — not just
# in the blobs. Without this, git's core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks these
# out with CRLF and `scp`/`sftp` ships them exactly as they sit on disk.
#
# deploy_cerbo.py also strips CR on upload, so a checkout with the wrong
# settings still deploys correctly. Both, on purpose: this one is silent and
# easy to lose.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.ini   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.CFG   text eol=lf
run     text eol=lf

*.pyc   binary
